hdMoonray: read moonray:visible_* primvars on first sync, not just post-forceInvisible

GeometryMixin::restoreVisibility had an early-return guard
(if (!mForcedInvisible) return;) that skipped reading the per-
component visibility primvars on visible rprims that hadn't
been previously force-invisible. Per-component visibility flags
(moonray:visible_in_camera / visible_shadow / etc.) only reached
RDL2 if the rprim went through an invisible→visible transition
during IPR. One-shot batch renders silently ignored the authored
primvars and used RDL2 defaults (all true).

Surfaced in GafferMoonray Phase 5-A: IECoreMoonray::Attributes
translates Cortex moonray:visibility:<component> into
moonray:visible_* primvars on the rprim, but they didn't reach
the RdlMeshGeometry body in the RDLA dump.

Fix: drop the early return, always re-read on the visible branch.
Cost: 9 GetPrimvar calls per visibility-dirty cycle. Negligible.

Apply path: hdMoonray submodule (scope: hdMoonray).

